# `tailwind-resolver` generates src/generated/tailwindcss/types.ts by embedding
# CSS values in TypeScript string literals. It escapes LF as `\n` but leaves CR
# untouched, so a CRLF input CSS produces a raw carriage return inside a string
# literal. That is invalid TypeScript, and because a program with syntax errors
# gets no semantic checking at all, a single CRLF in the CSS silently disables
# type checking for the whole project.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true here, so without this rule the working copy of the CSS
# is CRLF again on the next checkout and the generated file breaks again.
*.css text eol=lf
